3 A first look at OpenFOAM
From Tutorial 2 you will run turbulent channel-flow simulations in OpenFOAM. As a preview, turbulence modelling is configured in constant/turbulenceProperties:


constant/turbulenceProperties

/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
| =========                 |                                                 |
| \\      /  F ield         | OpenFOAM: The Open Source CFD Toolbox           |
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      turbulenceProperties;
}

simulationType  RAS;

RAS
{
1    RASModel        kOmegaSST;
    turbulence      on;
2    printCoeffs     on;
}


1

The turbulence model — we will compare kOmegaSST and kEpsilon later in the course.

2

Prints the model coefficients to the log at startup, useful for reproducibility.








